      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "example"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Illustrative example.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " A cosmetics brand wants videos for its ads. Creator A has the largest audience, but their product videos are static shots with no demonstration. Creator B has a modest audience, always shows the application gesture and offers three hooks. Creator C is close to the target audience but their sound is inaudible without music. For a UGC order the grid points to B: A’s audience will not be used, and C’s weakness sits on a priority criterion."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2,
          "id": "signals-that-should-give-you-pause"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Signals that should give you pause"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "warning"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "A portfolio showing only one kind of video, with no product demonstration."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Audience figures the Creator cannot or will not explain."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "A refusal to put deliverables, deadlines or usage rights in writing."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "No question about your brief, even when it leaves points open."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "None of these signals is disqualifying on its own. Together, they usually announce a difficult collaboration."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2,
          "id": "inside-avyor"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Inside AVYOR"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When AVYOR suggests a profile for your campaign, it shows the reasons behind the match: specialisation in your niche, presence on your target platforms, engagement rate, location and language, trust score, recent activity. Those reasons complement reading a portfolio, they do not replace it. You can then build a shortlist among the applications you receive before deciding; the decision remains yours."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
